# Security headers — served by GitHub Pages from this static file.
# GitHub Pages supports Netlify-style header files in the deployable
# directory: Netlify _headers in the root of public/ (copied verbatim
# into dist/) and Cloudflare headers.md (Markdown-style with ``` headers
# fences, no per-path globs). Astro middleware does not run on Pages.
#
# Paths mirror dist/ — the site is static: the device page is index.html,
# the 404 page is 404.html, robots.txt sits at the root, everything else
# lives under /assets/ and /_astro/. Per-path rules beat the wildcard
# below, so HTML documents get a 'self'-scoped CSP while asset responses
# get a no-scripts CSP. A single wildcard could not serve both.
#
# The DEV-only /editor route is stripped from production builds by
# astro.config.mjs (editorStrip integration), so no /editor/ rule is
# needed here. The dev server still serves it locally, but that is not
# the deployable directory.
#
# On the sub-path deployment (retvil.github.io/sdinc.dev/, see
# astro.config.mjs comment A) the paths in this file still match,
# because Pages serves them relative to the deploy root, not the host.
# CSP's self-references (self, 'self', data:) resolve against the
# document URL and stay correct at any base.

/
X-Frame-Options: DENY
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()

/assets/
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; script-src 'none'; style-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/_astro/
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; img-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; script-src 'none'; style-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'

# Static HTML documents: the device UI + the 404 page. 'self'-scoped CSP
# (no inline <script> — Astro ships separate .js files; data: icon is the
# only inline payload). COOP/COEP make cross-origin isolations available
# if the device ever adopts SharedArrayBuffer — harmless today since no
# cross-origin resource is loaded.
/*.html
Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
X-Frame-Options: DENY
X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
